# File field — `DisplayInfo` on the `FileEntity`, not on `FileId`

Incident: `ServiceRequestAttachment` upload `POST /File/upload/.../File` threw «فیلد موجودیت یافت نشد» because `[DisplayInfo(SystemType.File)]` sat on `FileId`. Entity metadata only indexes properties that have `[DisplayInfo]`. `FileController.Upload` looks up `entityPropName` in that list.

Form Builder already emits the correct pair (`FormBuilderCodeGenerator`, `SystemType.File`). Copy that. Canonical live shape: `Edms/Document.cs` (`MainFile` / `MainFileId`).

## Must

```csharp
[DisplayName("فایل")]
[DisplayInfo(null, true, type: SystemType.File)]
[ForeignKey(nameof(FileId))]
public virtual FileEntity? File { get; set; }

public long? FileId { get; set; }
```

```cshtml
<fileuploader bind="fileId" file-id="@Model?.FileId" file-entity="@Model?.File"
              label="فایل" entity-type="@typeof(Entity).FullName" entity-prop-name="File"
              max-file-size="20" accepted-file-types=".pdf,.zip,.png,.jpg,.jpeg"></fileuploader>
```

| Piece | Value |
|---|---|
| `[DisplayInfo]` + `[DisplayName]` + `fileTypes` / `maxFileSize` | Navigation `File` (`FileEntity`) |
| Database column | `FileId` (`long?`), no `[DisplayInfo]` |
| `entity-prop-name` / `data-entity-prop-name` | Navigation name (`File`, `MainFile`, …) |
| `bind` and `data-bind` | `{Name}Id` (`fileId`, `mainFileId`) |

`fileTypes` and `maxFileSize` on that `[DisplayInfo]` are what `FileController` enforces. The tag helper `accepted-file-types` / `max-file-size` are the same limits on the client.

## Must not

- `[DisplayInfo(SystemType.File)]` on `FileId` or any `long?` foreign key.
- `entity-prop-name="FileId"` (or `data-entity-prop-name="FileId"`). The upload URL must be the navigation name metadata actually contains.
- A `FileEntity` navigation with no `[DisplayInfo]` while the uploader sends that name.
